  "id": "DrugBank_DB01030 - MONDO_17327",
  "verbalization": "Topotecan is implicated in the treatment of various ovarian malignancies through a shared pathway involving Altretamine, which acts as a mediator in the therapeutic effect. The evidence suggests that Topotecan, through its indication for ovarian adenocarcinoma and mucinous adenocarcinoma, leads to the induction of Altretamine, which in turn is indicated for primary non-gestational choriocarcinoma of the ovary. This chain of indications implies a potential mechanism where Topotecan may influence the biological pathways that lead to the development or progression of choriocarcinoma, possibly through the activation of similar molecular targets or regulatory mechanisms. The recurring involvement of Altretamine in this chain suggests a possible role in the therapeutic response or pathophysiology of the disease. While the exact mechanism remains unclear, the integrated evidence points to a possible relationship between Topotecan and the primary non-gestational choriocarcinoma of the ovary, mediated by Altretamine.",
